### API Gateway Redis-Backed Distributed Rate Limiting Playground
### Gateway runs on http://localhost:8080 (Single Entry Point)

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ==========================================================================
### 1. OBTAIN JWT TOKEN (For user-specific rate limiting bucket)
### ==========================================================================

### 1.1 Login as Demo User
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "demo-user",
  "password": "user_demo_password_123"
}

### Capture user token
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### ==========================================================================
### 2. NORMAL QUOTA CONSUMPTION (Expects 200 OK + Rate-Limit Headers)
### ==========================================================================

### 2.1 Authenticated Request (Key resolved as "user:<userId>")
### Inspect response headers:
###   X-RateLimit-Replenish-Rate: 10
###   X-RateLimit-Burst-Capacity: 20
###   X-RateLimit-Remaining: 19
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.2 Anonymous / Unauthenticated Request (Key resolved as "ip:<remoteIp>")
### Falls back to client remote socket IP
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json

### ==========================================================================
### 3. ANTI-SPOOFING VERIFICATION
### ==========================================================================

### 3.1 Unauthenticated request attempting to inject X-User-Id
### The gateway MUST ignore "X-User-Id: victim" and rate-limit by client IP instead.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
X-User-Id: victim-account-id
Accept: application/json

### ==========================================================================
### 4. QUOTA EXHAUSTION / BURST FLOOD SIMULATION
### ==========================================================================

### Execute these in rapid succession (>20 requests in <1 second)
### The first 20 requests will succeed (burstCapacity = 20).
### Subsequent requests will immediately receive:
### HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
### Downstream microservices (catalog-service) will NOT receive excess traffic.

# Request Burst 01
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###
# Request Burst 02
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###
# Request Burst 03
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###
# Request Burst 04
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###
# Request Burst 05
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
